complete_reproduction_plan:
  paper_info:
    title: "Neural Posterior Score Estimation for Simulation-Based Inference"
    core_contribution: >
      Reproduce NPSE and sequential TSNPSE, score-based diffusion models that learn
      the score of the perturbed posterior directly by denoising score matching, and
      use probability-flow ODE sampling for likelihood-free Bayesian inference.

  file_structure: |
    project_root/
      README.md                              # LAST: usage, results, limitations
      requirements.txt                       # LAST: exact dependencies
      configs/
        defaults.yaml                        # SDE, architecture, training, budgets
      src/
        __init__.py
        sde.py                               # VE SDE, VP SDE, marginals, score of p_t|0
        score_networks.py                    # theta/x embeddings, time embedding, score net
        losses.py                            # DSM objectives for NPSE, SNPSE-A/B/C, NLSE, prior score
        probability_flow.py                  # ODE sampling and log-density via change of variables
        density.py                           # density evaluation helpers, Hutchinson trace estimator
        truncation.py                        # HPR_epsilon estimation and truncated proposal sampling
        training.py                          # train loops, early stopping, standardisation
        algorithms/
          __init__.py
          npse.py                            # Non-sequential NPSE
          tsnpse.py                          # Main sequential TSNPSE
          snpse_a.py                         # SNPSE-A with SIR correction
          snpse_b.py                         # SNPSE-B with weighted DSM
          snpse_c.py                         # SNPSE-C with proposal-prior score correction
          nlse.py                            # Neural Likelihood Score Estimation
          prior_score.py                     # Prior score estimation / closed-form prior score
        utils/
          __init__.py
          metrics.py                         # C2ST, MMD, posterior predictive checks
          sbibm_utils.py                     # wrap sbibm tasks and baselines
      tasks/
        __init__.py
        base.py                              # task API: prior.sample/log_prob, simulator
        gaussian_linear.py
        gaussian_mixture.py
        two_moons.py
        gaussian_linear_uniform.py
        bernoulli_glm.py
        slcp.py
        sir.py
        lotka_volterra.py
        pyloric.py                           # optional real-world simulator wrapper
      experiments/
        run_npse_benchmarks.py
        run_tsnpse_benchmarks.py
        run_sequential_variants.py
        run_nlse_comparison.py
        run_pyloric.py
        evaluate_benchmarks.py
        plot_results.py
      tests/
        test_sde.py
        test_score_training.py
        test_probability_flow.py
        test_truncation.py
        test_tasks.py

  implementation_components: |
    1. SDE MODULE (`src/sde.py`)
       Implement abstract SDE with:
       - drift f(theta, t)
       - diffusion g(t)
       - marginal transition p_{t|0}(theta_t | theta_0)
       - grad_{theta_t} log p_{t|0}(theta_t | theta_0)
       VE SDE:
         f=0
         g(t)=sigma_min*(sigma_max/sigma_min)^t*sqrt(2*log(sigma_max/sigma_min))
         p_t|0 = N(theta_t | theta_0, sigma_min^2*(sigma_max/sigma_min)^{2t} I)
         score = -(theta_t - theta_0) / var
         sigma_min = 0.01 for 2D tasks/SIR/Two Moons, 0.05 otherwise.
         sigma_max via Technique 1 of Song & Ermon 2020.
       VP SDE:
         beta_t = beta_min + t*(beta_max-beta_min)
         f(theta,t) = -0.5*beta_t*theta
         g(t) = sqrt(beta_t)
         beta_min=0.1, beta_max=11.0
         mean = theta_0*exp(-0.5*integral_0^t beta_s ds)
         var = 1 - exp(-integral_0^t beta_s ds)
         score = -(theta_t - mean) / var
       Also implement integral beta_t closed-form: ∫_0^t beta_s ds = 0.1t + 5.45t^2.

    2. SCORE NETWORK (`src/score_networks.py`)
       Architecture exactly as in Appendix E.3.2:
       - theta embedding: 3-layer FC MLP, 256 hidden units/layer, input d,
         output max(30, 4*d).
       - x embedding: 3-layer FC MLP, 256 hidden units/layer, input p,
         output max(30, 4*p).
       - time embedding: 64-dimensional sinusoidal embedding:
         for i<=32: sin(t / 10000^((i-1)/31))
         else: cos(t / 10000^(((i-32)-1)/31))
       - concatenate [theta_emb, x_emb, t_emb]
         feed to 3-layer FC MLP, 256 hidden units/layer, output dimension d.
       - SiLU activation between all layers.
       - standardise theta_t and x before network using dataset mean/std.

    3. LOSSES (`src/losses.py`)
       Core NPSE/TSNPSE DSM loss, Eq. (7):
         Loss(psi) = 1/2 E[
           lambda_t || s_psi(theta_t, x, t) - grad_{theta_t} log p_{t|0}(theta_t|theta_0) ||^2 ]
       where theta_0,x ~ p(theta,x)=p(theta)p(x|theta), t~U(0,T), theta_t ~ p_t|0.
       Implement configurable lambda_t. Paper does not specify exact lambda_t in excerpt;
       default recommended:
         VE: lambda_t = 1/g(t)^2
         VP: lambda_t = 1
       with override in configs/defaults.yaml.
       SNPSE-B weighted loss:
         Loss = E[ w(theta_0) || s_psi(theta_t,x,t) - grad log p_t|0 ||^2 ],
         w(theta_0)=p(theta_0)/tilde_p^r(theta_0).
       SNPSE-A/C use same unweighted DSM as NPSE but on proposal data:
         tilde_p^r(theta_0)=1/r sum_{s=0}^{r-1} p_psi^s(theta_0|x_obs),
         p_psi^0(...) = prior.
       NLSE likelihood-score loss, Eq. (57):
         Loss_lik = E[ || s_psi_lik(theta_t,x,t)
           + grad_theta log p_t(theta_t)
           - grad_theta log p_t|0(theta_t|theta_0) ||^2 ].
       Prior score estimation loss, Eq. (64):
         Loss_pri = E[ || s_psi_pri(theta_t,t) - grad_theta log p_t|0(theta_t|theta_0) ||^2 ].

    4. PROBABILITY FLOW ODE SAMPLING (`src/probability_flow.py`)
       Reverse-time probability flow ODE:
         dtheta_t/dt = f(theta_t,t) - 0.5*g(t)^2 * s_psi(theta_t, x_obs, t)
       Integrate from noise at t=T to posterior sample at t=0.
       Use RK45 (`scipy.integrate.solve_ivp` or `torchdiffeq`) as paper uses RK45.
       For density evaluation, use instantaneous change-of-variables formula (Eq. 5):
         log p_0(theta_0) = log p_T(theta_T) + ∫_0^T tr(∂v_psi/∂theta) dt
       where v_psi(theta,t) = f(theta,t) - 0.5*g(t)^2*s_psi(theta,x_obs,t).
       Implement exact trace via `torch.autograd.grad` and optional
       Hutchinson-Skilling trace estimator for speed.

    5. TRUNCATED PROPOSAL / HPR_EPSILON (`src/truncation.py`)
       After each TSNPSE round:
       - sample 20000 theta from current approximate posterior via probability-flow ODE.
       - compute approximate posterior log-density for each theta via change-of-variables.
       - threshold κ = epsilon-quantile of log densities, epsilon=5e-4.
       - proposal = prior restricted to {theta : log p_approx(theta|x_obs) > κ}.
       - sample proposal by rejection:
         a) cheap screening: accept only prior samples inside empirical hypercube
            of approximate posterior samples.
         b) compute log-density by ODE and accept only if > κ.
       This exactly follows Appendix E.3.3 and Deistler et al. 2022a Section 6.3.

    6. ALGORITHMS (`src/algorithms/`)
       NPSE (`npse.py`):
         - Sample theta_i ~ prior, x_i ~ simulator.
         - Add time t_i ~ U(0,T), theta_ti ~ p_t|0.
         - Train score network with DSM loss until early stopping.
         - Return sampler by solving probability-flow ODE at x_obs.

       TSNPSE (`tsnpse.py`), main algorithm:
         Inputs: x_obs, prior, simulator, budget N, rounds R=10, M=N/R.
         Dataset D = {}.
         For r=1..R:
           If r==1: theta_i ~ prior
           Else: theta_i ~ truncated proposal from HPR_epsilon of
                 previous approximate posterior.
           Simulate x_i ~ p(x|theta_i), add (theta_i,x_i) to D.
           Draw t_i ~ U(0,T), theta_ti ~ p_t|0(.|theta_i).
           Train tilt s_psi^r to approximate proposal posterior score:
             Loss = mean over D || s_psi^r(theta_t,x,t)
                    - grad log p_t|0(theta_t|theta_0) ||^2.
           Generate approximate posterior samples by solving probability-flow
             ODE with s_psi^r(theta_t,x_obs,t).
           Estimate HPR_epsilon for next round.
         Return final posterior sampler.

       SNPSE-A (`snpse_a.py`), Appendix C.2 / Algorithm 3:
         - Train proposal-posterior score on accumulated proposal data.
         - Sample M' >= M from proposal posterior.
         - SIR correction weights: h_i = p(theta_i) / tilde_p^r(theta_i).
         - Exact density-based weights only available for r=1,2 without extra
           proposal-prior approximation; implement exact first two rounds and optional
           KDE/flow proposal-prior approximation for later rounds.

       SNPSE-B (`snpse_b.py`), Appendix C.3 / Algorithm 4:
         - Train true posterior score directly using importance-weighted loss:
             w(theta_0) = p(theta_0)/tilde_p^r(theta_0).
         - No post-sampling correction needed.

       SNPSE-C (`snpse_c.py`), Appendix C.4 / Algorithm 5:
         - For r=1, tilde_s_psi^r = s_psi.
         - For r>1, train proposal-prior score network s_phi^r(theta_t,t),
           then define:
             tilde_s_psi^r(theta_t,x,t) =
               s_psi(theta_t,x,t)
               + s_phi^r(theta_t,t)
               - grad_theta log p_t(theta_t).
         - Train tilde_s_psi^r with DSM on proposal data.
         - Use recovered s_psi as approximation to true posterior score.

       NLSE (`nlse.py`), Appendix B:
         - Train likelihood score s_psi_lik with Eq. (57).
         - If perturbed prior score is closed form under VE SDE (uniform/Gaussian
           mixture priors), use automatic differentiation.
         - Else train prior score network with Algorithm 2.
         - Posterior score = likelihood score + perturbed prior score.

       Prior score closed forms, Appendix B.2.1:
         Under VE SDE with p_t|0 = N(theta_t|theta_0, tau_t^2 I):
           Uniform prior: product of Gaussian CDF differences.
           Gaussian mixture: mixture with inflated variances Sigma_i + tau_t^2 I.
         Use torch.autograd.grad to obtain scores.

    7. TASKS (`src/tasks/`)
       Implement benchmark simulators/priors as in Appendix E.1:
       - Gaussian Linear: p(theta)=N(0,0.1I), p(x|theta)=N(theta,0.1I), d=10.
       - Gaussian Mixture: theta~U(-10,10)^2,
         p(x|theta)=0.5 N(theta,I)+0.5 N(theta,0.01I).
       - Two Moons: prior U(-1,1)^2; likelihood from rotated crescent equations.
       - Gaussian Linear Uniform: theta~U(-1,1)^10, p(x|theta)=N(theta,0.1I).
       - Bernoulli GLM: 10D theta = (beta,f), beta~N(0,2),
         f~N(0, (F^T F)^(-1)), data are 10D sufficient statistics.
       - SLCP: theta~U(-3,3)^5, 8D Gaussian likelihood with nonlinear mean/cov.
       - SIR: theta=(beta,gamma), beta~LogNormal(log(0.4),0.5),
         gamma~LogNormal(log(0.8),0.2); simulator follows SIR ODE and
         Bin(1000, I/N) observations.
       - Lotka-Volterra: theta=(alpha,beta,gamma,delta), alpha,gamma~LogNormal(-0.125,0.5),
         beta,delta~LogNormal(-3,0.5); observations are 10 evenly spaced
         predator/prey counts.
       Prefer wrapping `sbibm` tasks where available for exact reference behavior;
       custom implementations should match sbibm outputs.
       Pyloric task (`tasks/pyloric.py`): 31 parameters, 18 summary statistics,
       uniform prior ranges from Prinz et al. 2004. Replace invalid summary stats
       with value two standard deviations below prior-predictive mean.

    8. TRAINING AND STANDARDISATION (`src/training.py`)
       Adam lr=1e-4.
       15% validation split; early stop if validation loss does not improve for 1000 steps;
       max 3000 training iterations.
       Batch sizes:
         simulation budget 1000 or 10000:
           non-sequential 50, sequential 200.
         simulation budget 100000:
           both 500.
       Standardise theta_t and x using per-dimension estimated mean/std.

  validation_approach: |
    1. UNIT TESTS
       - SDE transitions: empirical mean/covariance of VE/VP p_t|0 match closed forms.
       - Gradient scores: numerical gradient of log p_t|0 matches analytic score.
       - Probability-flow density: for a Gaussian toy posterior, sampled theta
         have empirical moments matching analytic posterior and density
         evaluation returns consistent log-likelihood values.
       - Truncation: HPR_epsilon threshold selects expected fraction 1-epsilon of
         approximate posterior samples.

    2. BENCHMARK EVALUATION
       - Use eight sbibm benchmark tasks and reference posteriors.
       - Simulation budgets: 1000, 10000, 100000.
       - Non-sequential NPSE: run 10 rounds? Actually NPSE is one round; train once per budget.
       - Sequential TSNPSE: R=10, M=N/R per round.
       - Compute C2ST between approximate posterior samples and reference posterior
         samples from sbibm. Also compute MMD and mean/var error if available.
       - Compare NPSE with NPE and TSNPSE with SNPE-C/TSNPE using sbibm baselines.
       - Expected results:
         - SLCP and Lotka-Volterra: TSNPSE/NPSE should outperform baselines,
           showing best accuracy or lower C2ST.
         - Remaining tasks: mixed ranking depending on task and simulation budget.
         - Both VE and VP SDEs should be evaluated; recommend VE for low-dimensional
           tasks and VP for high-dimensional tasks.

    3. SEQUENTIAL VARIANT CHECKS
       - Run TSNPSE, SNPSE-A, SNPSE-B, and SNPSE-C on SLCP and GLU.
       - Verify TSNPSE significantly outperforms SNPSE-A and SNPSE-B.
       - SNPSE-C often fails with C2ST near 1 due to proposal-prior score approximation;
         reproduce this behavior rather than expecting strong performance.

    4. NLSE COMPARISON
       - On four benchmarks (e.g., Gaussian Linear, Gaussian Mixture, Two Moons, GLM)
         compare NPSE and NLSE with VE SDE.
       - Expected: little difference when perturbed prior score is analytic,
         but NPSE outperforms NLSE when prior score must be estimated.

    5. REAL-WORLD PYLORIC EXPERIMENT
       - Apply TSNPSE with VP SDE, 9 rounds, 30000 initial simulations,
         20000 added simulations per round.
       - Replace invalid summary statistics as described.
       - Expected final round valid summary statistic percentage about 81%.
       - Posterior predictive samples should match observed voltage-trace summaries.
       - Pairwise marginals should be similar to those reported in the literature.
       - Compute simulation-based coverage calibration (SBCC); expected approximate
         coverage for mid-low confidence levels is below nominal confidence,
         with better calibration at high confidence levels.

    6. FIGURES
       - Reproduce analogues of Figures 2-4:
         benchmark C2ST tables/plots for non-sequential and sequential methods,
         posterior predictive check for pyloric, valid summary rate vs simulations.

  environment_setup: |
    - Python 3.9 or 3.10.
    - PyTorch >= 2.0.
    - `sbibm` for benchmark tasks, reference posteriors, and baseline algorithms.
    - `scipy` for RK45/ODE integration, `torchdiffeq` optional for GPU ODE solving.
    - `numpy`, `pandas`, `matplotlib`, `scikit-learn` for metrics/plots.
    - `tqdm` for progress bars, `PyYAML` for configs, `pytest` for tests.
    - GPU strongly recommended for benchmark and pyloric experiments.
    - Pyloric real-world experiment requires access to the stomatogastric simulator
      and observed data, e.g., as used in Prinz et al. 2004 / Gonçalves et al. 2020
      or the corresponding sbibm task if available.
    - Exact package list should be fixed in `requirements.txt` only after core code
      is implemented and tested.

  implementation_strategy: |
    Phase 1: Core SDE and score network
      - Implement `src/sde.py` with VE/VP transitions and analytic scores.
      - Implement `src/score_networks.py` with the exact embedding/score architecture.
      - Write tests for SDE marginal statistics and gradient correctness.

    Phase 2: Non-sequential NPSE
      - Implement `src/losses.py` with NPSE DSM loss.
      - Implement `src/training.py` with Adam, validation split, early stopping,
        standardisation, and batching rules.
      - Implement `src/algorithms/npse.py`.
      - Validate on Gaussian Linear and Two Moons against analytic/reference posterior.

    Phase 3: Probability-flow sampling and density evaluation
      - Implement `src/probability_flow.py` for reverse ODE sampling and
        exact/estimated log-density via change-of-variables.
      - Test density on a simple Gaussian posterior and compare with analytic log-prob.

    Phase 4: TSNPSE with truncated proposals
      - Implement `src/truncation.py` with HPR_epsilon and rejection sampling.
      - Implement `src/algorithms/tsnpse.py`.
      - Test on Two Moons and SLCP. Confirm iterative narrowing of posterior and
        improved C2ST with rounds.

    Phase 5: Sequential variants and NLSE
      - Implement `src/algorithms/snpse_a.py`, `snpse_b.py`, `snpse_c.py`.
      - Implement `src/algorithms/prior_score.py` and `src/algorithms/nlse.py`.
      - Run SLCP/GLU comparisons for variant sanity checks.

    Phase 6: Benchmark suite integration
      - Implement or wrap all eight `src/tasks/` benchmark environments.
      - Run NPSE and TSNPSE for budgets [1000, 10000, 100000].
      - Use `src/utils/metrics.py` to compute C2ST/MMD and compare with sbibm baselines.
      - Generate benchmark figures.

    Phase 7: Pyloric experiment
      - Implement `src/tasks/pyloric.py` and invalid summary replacement.
      - Run TSNPSE with 9 rounds/initial 30000/20000 per round using VP SDE.
      - Compute valid summary rate, posterior predictive quality, SBCC coverage,
        and pairwise marginal plots.

    Phase 8: Documentation and finalization
      - Add `README.md` with reproduction instructions and expected results.
      - Pin dependencies in `requirements.txt`.
      - Run full test suite and smoke-test all entry points.

    Missing-detail defaults:
      - lambda_t weighting is not explicitly specified in the available text; expose
        `loss_weighting` in config and default to VE=1/g(t)^2, VP=1.
      - If exact pyloric simulator is unavailable, mark as optional and focus benchmark
        reproduction first.
      - For SNPSE-A beyond two rounds, use a KDE/normalising-flow proposal-prior density
        or restrict experiments to the first two rounds as per the paper's exact computation.
